    4087	### D31 — Adiprasito-Huh-Katz combinatorial Hodge theory of an arithmetic prime-matroid
    4088	
    4089	**Question:** Adiprasito-Huh-Katz 2018 *Annals* 188, 381 (= arXiv:1511.02888)
    4090	proved the **hard Lefschetz theorem** and **Hodge-Riemann relations** for
    4091	the Chow ring `A^*(M)` of an arbitrary matroid `M`, settling the
    4092	**Heron-Rota-Welsh conjecture**: the absolute values of the coefficients
    4093	of the reduced characteristic polynomial `\bar{χ}_M(t) = χ_M(t)/(t − 1)`
    4094	form a **log-concave sequence** for *every* matroid (realisable or not).
    4095	**Question:** define an **arithmetic prime-matroid** `M_P^N` whose
    4096	characteristic polynomial encodes `χ_P` data — for instance, the matroid
    4097	on ground set `[2, N]` whose **flats** are the ideals
    4098	`(d) ∩ [2, N]` for `d | \mathrm{rad}(\prod_{p ≤ N} p)`, equivalently the
    4099	`gcd`-closed sublattice of the divisibility poset; or the
    4100	**transversal matroid** with blocks `B_p = \{n ∈ [2, N] : p | n\}` for
    4101	each prime `p ≤ N`. AHK gives **log-concavity of `|μ_{M_P^N}(F)|`**
    4102	across the lattice of flats — does the log-concavity inequality
    4103	`|μ_k|^2 ≥ |μ_{k-1}| \cdot |μ_{k+1}|` (where `μ_k` = signed Möbius
    4104	coefficient at corank `k`) yield a **sharp prime-counting inequality**
    4105	sharper than the Hardy-Littlewood / Brun / Selberg sieve bounds at
    4106	the singular-series level?
    4107	
    4108	**Why frontier:** AHK's proof is one of the most celebrated results in
    4109	combinatorics of the past decade and it has **never** been applied to
    4110	an arithmetic matroid encoding the prime indicator. The Heron-Rota-Welsh
    4111	log-concavity is a NEW kind of inequality on signed sums of arithmetic
    4112	Möbius values — it constrains the partial sums of `μ(d) χ_P`-like
    4113	quantities in ways that the standard Selberg/Brun upper-bound machinery
    4114	does not. **A successful AHK-application would be a publishable
    4115	analytic-NT inequality** at the intersection of matroid theory and
    4116	prime-counting. The **non-realisable** branch of AHK matters here:
