    # Three Matroid Definitions
    
    ## (1) Characteristic Polynomial via Möbius Function
    
    The characteristic polynomial is defined as:
    
    **Formula:** "p_M(λ) := ∑_A μ(∅,A)λ^(r(E)−r(A))" where the sum ranges over all flats A of the matroid.
    
    The μ symbol denotes the "Möbius function of the geometric lattice of the matroid."
    
    ## (2) Whitney Rank Generating Function
    
    This polynomial captures rank information across all subsets:
    
    **Formula:** "R_M(u,v) = ∑_(S⊆E) u^(r(M)−r(S)) v^(|S|−r(S))"
    
    The document notes this expresses the "co-rank-nullity or rank generating polynomial," where exponents track the corank and nullity (size minus rank) of each subset S.
    
    ## (3) Transversal Matroid
    
    For a bipartite graph G = (U, V, E), one forms a matroid where "the elements are vertices on one side U of the bipartition, and the independent subsets are sets of endpoints of matchings of the graph."
    
    The rank function corresponds to maximum matching size: an independent set has size |U| if there exist |U| vertex-disjoint paths connecting it to matching endpoints.
